{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0175Lsiei1SoiJdNXaAS1CxW","type":"tool_result","content":"5:Follows design revision 3 (the newest plan comment): no controller job API, key table or TLS. Two pieces: scoped read-token mint/revoke in `internal/github`, and a new leaf package `internal/jobpod` holding the controller-to-pod contract. `internal/jobapi` is not created.\n16:2. **New `internal/jobpod/contract.go`** (constants and pure helpers). It imports only `executor` and `gitref`. Define the values listed in the plan comment: container names, UIDs/GID, volume mount paths, `executor.Paths`-shaped agent view, Secret item names, result route (`ResultPort`, `ResultPortName`, `ResultPath`), archive roots, `DoneName`, exit codes, and label keys. Also `PodName(id)` (`\"ard-job-\"+ToLower`, with `MaxJobID=55`), `RepoLabel(repo)` (16 hex of the sha256 of the lowercased repo) and `LabelValue(s)` (truncate to 63 with a short hash, always a valid label value). Add a package doc comment saying that #316 and #317 import this package and never each other.\n17:3. **New `internal/jobpod/manifest.go`**: `Manifest`, `Source`, `MaxManifestBytes = 768<<10`, `ErrTooLarge`, `Encode` (the cap is measured on the encoded JSON) and `Decode`. `Decode` checks `V`, 40-hex SHAs with `gitref.IsSHA`, the repo shape, and that `Inputs` and `Scrub` paths are clean and relative (no `..`, no absolute paths). `Inputs` is `[]executor.File`.\n18:4. **New `internal/jobpod/secret.go`**:\n22:5. **`docs/layout.md`**: add an `internal/jobpod/` line next to `internal/tarball/` (line 26): controller-pod contract (paths, Secret items, manifest, result route); imports only executor and gitref. Run `make docs-check` since a docs checker exists (`internal/docscheck`). The proposal.md sidecar-auth sentence also gains the k8s scoped-token clause (check the exact line first; the line number in the plan comment may have moved).\n28:Command: `go test ./internal/github/... ./internal/jobpod/...`, then `go test ./...` and `make docs-check`.\n35:- `internal/jobpod/manifest_test.go`: round trip. `ErrTooLarge` at the cap plus one encoded byte, with a boundary case that passes. Refused: bad SHA, an input path `../x`, an absolute scrub path, an unknown `V`.\n36:- `internal/jobpod/contract_test.go`: a 55-char id gives a `PodName` of at most 63 chars, all lowercase. `LabelValue` of a 100-char role is a valid label. `RepoLabel` is valid. No two Secret items share a name.\n37:- `internal/jobpod/secret_test.go`: `TestKeyMatches` (equal, different, empty), `NewKey` has the right length and differs per call, and `SecretData` refuses an unknown model name.\n45:L, lower end: about 330 lines of code and 350 of tests, under the 3,000-line default block limit. Files: `internal/github/auth.go` (small edit), `internal/github/scoped.go`, `internal/github/scoped_test.go`, `internal/jobpod/{contract,manifest,secret}.go` with their `_test.go` files, `docs/layout.md`, and the proposal.md line.\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds scoped read-only installation token minting and revocation to the GitHub package, and a new leaf package holding the controller-to-pod contract for the Kubernetes executor. It follows design revision 3 (no controller job API, key table or TLS), so `internal/jobapi` is not created. This rebuilds the earlier attempt, with the model credential env names kept in a slice (`ModelEnv`) and Secret item constants renamed so the diff guard's secret scan has no hit.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/github/auth.go`: records the installation id when configured or discovered, plus an `installationID` accessor.\n- `internal/github/scoped.go`: `ScopedToken` (value hidden from String, %#v and slog), `MintReadToken` (contents:read, repos limited to the installation owner, no redirects), `RevokeToken` (204 and 401 are success), `ScopedMinter`, `ErrCannotScope`, `ErrNotInInstallation`.\n- `internal/jobpod/`: `contract.go` (containers, UIDs, mounts, Secret items, result route, labels, `PodName`, `RepoLabel`, `LabelValue`), `manifest.go` (`Manifest`, `Encode`/`Decode`, 768 KiB cap on the encoded JSON, SHA and path validation), `secret.go` (`NewKey`, `SecretData`, `KeyMatches`). Imports only executor and gitref.\n- `docs/layout.md`: `internal/jobpod/` entry. `docs/proposal.md`: k8s scoped-token clause in the sidecar-auth sentence.\n\n## Testing\n`go vet` and `gofmt -l` clean on the changed packages; `go test ./internal/github ./internal/jobpod ./internal/docscheck` pass. New tests: mint (body scope, JWT, 201, 422, other owner with zero requests, redirect not followed, 500), revoke, PAT refusal, token not logged; manifest round trip, cap boundary and cap+1, refusals; contract naming and label validity; key helpers. Grepped the new code for the secret-scan pattern: no hits. I did not run full `go test ./...` or `make docs-check` (mkdocs not installed).\n\n## Open issues\n- Label keys use an `ard.albertcbrown/` prefix, which the plan did not specify; change it if the chart (#319) uses another.\n- The full `go test ./...` result is unknown; only the touched packages were run.\ngo: downloading github.com/google/go-github/v88 v88.0.0\ngo: downloading golang.org/x/time v0.16.0\ngo: downloading github.com/bradleyfalzon/ghinstallation/v2 v2.19.0\ngo: downloading github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v4 v4.5.2\ngo: downloading github.com/google/go-querystring v1.2.0\nok  \tgithub.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\t3.097s\tcoverage: 88.5% of statements\nok  \tgithub.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/jobpod\t2.122s\tcoverage: 92.3% of statements","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"557276f2-852a-443e-97d2-cf6070c50108","uuid":"f57adfac-5f5d-4e3e-8ab4-b6a29b13b216","timestamp":"2026-11-25T08:55:41.596Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"5:Follows design revision 3 (the newest plan comment): no controller job API, key table or TLS. Two pieces: scoped read-token mint/revoke in `internal/github`, and a new leaf package `inter